WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:01.499
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.499 --> 00:00:03.800
- The first time I met Miss Louise?

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.566
Never shall forget it.

00:00:05.566 --> 00:00:07.763
We met eye to eye, you know,

00:00:07.763 --> 00:00:08.679
and that must've been

00:00:08.679 --> 00:00:10.346
love at first sight.

00:00:13.471 --> 00:00:15.661
- [Narrator] This is Charles "LaLa" Evans.

00:00:15.661 --> 00:00:18.359
- All right, here we go. (laughs)

00:00:18.359 --> 00:00:19.734
- [Narrator] He and his wife Louise lived

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:23.586
in this house in Starkville, Mississippi.

00:00:23.586 --> 00:00:27.003
- We were married 59 years and 11 months.

00:00:28.036 --> 00:00:30.446
And we were one month shy of 60 years.

00:00:30.446 --> 00:00:31.946
We almost made 60.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.436
- [Narrator] After she died, LaLa created

00:00:34.436 --> 00:00:36.436
a unique tribute to her.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.496
- I decided I'd do this in memory of her.

00:00:41.496 --> 00:00:44.913
And we call this LaLa and Louise's Place.

00:00:45.846 --> 00:00:48.560
- [Narrator] It's his
personal memorial to Louise

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.143
made up of thousands of photos.

00:00:52.331 --> 00:00:53.414
- This is it.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.577
This is it.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.360
Everywhere we went we
took pictures, you know.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:00.984
"You stand over there, that
oughta make a good one."

00:01:00.984 --> 00:01:02.647
"You stand over here,
that'll make a good one."

00:01:02.647 --> 00:01:04.136
"Hold it, hold it, hold it."

00:01:04.136 --> 00:01:06.623
Click! (laughs)

00:01:06.623 --> 00:01:08.673
We had talked about it before she passed

00:01:08.673 --> 00:01:10.523
that one day we wanna build a museum

00:01:10.523 --> 00:01:12.606
to put these pictures in.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.659
We didn't get a chance to do that,

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:18.036
but the idea never left my mind

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:21.036
and so I said I'm gon' do it anyway.

00:01:22.842 --> 00:01:24.009
This was 1968.

00:01:25.532 --> 00:01:28.242
We were goin' dancin' somewhere.

00:01:28.242 --> 00:01:31.218
Back in those days
dancin' was a big thing.

00:01:31.218 --> 00:01:33.590
When I first met my
wife she couldn't dance

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.242
and she just got tired of that.

00:01:35.242 --> 00:01:37.505
She said, "You gon'
teach me how to do that."

00:01:37.505 --> 00:01:41.382
And after I taught her we
were such a smooth couple,

00:01:41.382 --> 00:01:44.465
you know, we didn't miss a beat, man.

00:01:46.302 --> 00:01:48.385
This is my 33 collection.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.840
Four Tops, look at that, the Four Tops.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:52.923
Ohio Players.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:54.962
45 city.

00:01:54.962 --> 00:01:55.795
- [Narrator] Would you and Louise dance

00:01:55.795 --> 00:01:57.280
to some of these records?

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:58.880
- Oh man, yeah.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:01:59.953
Did we?

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.680
(laughs) Shoot.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.680
Yes, we did.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:06.416
(somber orchestral music)

00:02:06.416 --> 00:02:09.083
This right here, our last dance.

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.914
I'll never forget it.

00:02:13.989 --> 00:02:15.156
It was in July

00:02:16.727 --> 00:02:17.989
and I took her,

00:02:17.989 --> 00:02:21.480
spinned her around, dipped
her for the last time,

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.530
brought her back up, (kissing smack)

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:26.280
put one of them on her, you know?

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:32.734
The following Friday is when
she had a massive heart attack

00:02:33.967 --> 00:02:37.217
and she wasn't responding, you know.

00:02:37.217 --> 00:02:40.593
All of a sudden she looked up at me

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.510
and said, "I love you,"

00:02:43.387 --> 00:02:44.720
and that was it.

00:02:52.377 --> 00:02:53.210
Okay.

00:02:54.226 --> 00:02:56.059
Changin' of the guard.

00:02:57.638 --> 00:02:58.910
We had such a beautiful life.

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:01.296
I got so much to remember

00:03:01.296 --> 00:03:04.110
and I'm just livin' a beautiful memory.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:04.943
Yeah.

